# FD merge metric failure analysis v1

Status: post-outcome evaluator diagnosis. The failed audit attempt and its
original inputs remain immutable. This note does not change the frozen data,
arms, widths, primary norm-loss definition, projection metric, or hypothesis.

## Observed failure

`audit-fd-merge-topology-v1` failed at the assertion equating
`discarded_mass_from_norm` with `accumulated_discarded_mass` for a merge arm.
For `ell=32`, balanced merging reported 0.0362063117 from the final norm loss
but only 0.0317927833 from summed shrink thresholds. The analogous left-deep
values were 0.0411400851 and 0.0372706052. Central row-stream FD retained the
expected equality to roundoff.

## Cause

For a row-stream FD shrink of a full `ell x d` buffer, subtracting
`delta = sigma_ell^2` from all `ell` squared singular values leaves one zero
row, so the Frobenius norm loss divided by `ell` equals `delta`.

For a merge, however, the input is a `2 ell x d` stack. Keeping only the first
`ell` singular directions after the same subtraction gives

`(||C||_F^2 - ||B||_F^2) / ell
 = delta + (1/ell) * sum_{i>ell} sigma_i(C)^2`.

The second term is the energy of the truncated lower half. Therefore the sum of
thresholds is not the total discarded norm mass for merge trees. The producer's
final norm-loss field remains the prospectively declared primary measurement;
the threshold sum is a separate diagnostic and was mislabeled as if an identity
held.

## Repair contract

The v2 audit will independently reconstruct every topology and retain four
separate checks: covariance equivalence of reconstructed sketches, summed
threshold equivalence, shrink-count equivalence, and total norm-loss equivalence
including merge-tail energy. It will apply the frozen balanced-versus-left-deep
falsifier to the norm-derived total discarded mass and projection cost. No raw
result is overwritten and no new data or favorable tolerance is introduced.
